        }
      ],
      "content": "runlet, a cask or vessel of varying capacity; the quantity of liquor contained in this (large runlets appear usually to have varied between 12 and 18½ gallons, small ones between a pint or quart and 3 or 4 gallons) (OED s.v. runlet1) | as a packing unit for dry goods of no particular size | as a packing unit for wine | as a measure of granum | cask, a transport unit for liquid goods | meaning unknown"
    }
